{
  $schema: 'https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json',
  // ── Renovate HOLDS registry ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A durable, reasoned blacklist of releases that must NOT be applied, with the
  // WHY recorded right next to the enforcement. The Tier-4 upgrade-shepherd agent
  // reads this file before working any PR (so it never re-investigates a known
  // bad upgrade); Renovate enforces it directly (so the held PR stops churning).
  //
  // Each hold is a packageRule that does two things:
  //   • ENFORCES via `allowedVersions` — a semver range that excludes the bad
  //     version(s). Where a FIXED release is known, the range RE-OPENS at it
  //     automatically (e.g. '<2.3.2 || >=3.0.0' skips 2.3.2–2.x and resumes at
  //     3.0.0). Where the resume condition is NOT a version of THIS package (e.g.
  //     "after a different component is upgraded"), use a plain upper bound and
  //     lift the hold by hand.
  //   • DOCUMENTS via `description` (array of strings — Renovate-legal, shown in
  //     logs/PRs, greppable by the agent). Convention, one entry per line:
  //       'HELD <pkg> <range> — <one-line summary>'
  //       'Reason: <why it breaks>'
  //       'Issue: <upstream tracking URL>'
  //       'Resume: <condition> (auto | manual)'
  //       'Recorded: <YYYY-MM-DD> by <who>. Related: <PR/issue/memory refs>'
  //
  // TO ADD a hold: append a packageRule following the convention, set the
  //   tightest `allowedVersions` that blocks the bad release, validate with
  //   `npx --yes --package renovate renovate-config-validator .renovate/holds.json5`,
  //   commit.
  // TO LIFT a hold: delete its packageRule (or widen `allowedVersions`) in a
  //   commit that references the upstream resolution, then let Renovate re-propose.
  //
  // holds.json5 extends LAST in renovate.json5, so an `allowedVersions` block
  // here is the final word for the package even if an allowlist would auto-merge it.
  // ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  packageRules: [
    {
      description: [
        'HELD suspended one-shot synthetic NFS capsule: image/helper/template stay immutable.',
        'Resume: remove only in reviewed capsule retirement after actual init/main termination and protected Pod/worker evidence. Execution is a separate reviewed suspend-only change.',
      ],
      matchFileNames: ['kubernetes/main/apps/dev-agents/gasha01-nfs-synthetic-1010/app/job-*.yaml'],
      enabled: false,
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD ARC Docker DinD: update the sidecar and its exact-image PolicyException together, by hand.',
        'Reason: the Kubernetes image manager finds the DinD image in the shared runner component but does not find the bare image-list entry in the Kyverno exception. Updating only the component makes all four Docker runner pools fail baseline admission.',
        'Issue: https://github.com/thaynes43/haynes-ops/pull/3503#discussion_r4203251469',
        'Resume: MANUAL — update kubernetes/shared/components/arc/dind/helmrelease.yaml and kubernetes/main/apps/kyverno/policies/app/exceptions/arc-dind.yaml atomically, then verify admission and real Docker workflows. Re-enable automation only when both references share one tested update path.',
        'Recorded: 2026-10-07 by Codex during the ARC infrastructure review. Runbook: .agents/runbooks/self-hosted-runners.md.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['docker', 'docker.io/docker', 'docker.io/library/docker'],
      matchFileNames: [
        'kubernetes/shared/components/arc/dind/**',
        'kubernetes/main/apps/kyverno/policies/app/exceptions/arc-dind.yaml',
      ],
      enabled: false,
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/postgresql majors: track the running postgres16 cluster major — Postgres 17 lands only as a deliberate cluster migration, never a Renovate merge.',
        'Reason: the image has two consumers that must move TOGETHER with the cluster: (1) cluster16.yaml `imageName` — a CNPG major upgrade is a real migration (dump/restore or blue-green per CNPG docs), not an in-place bump; (2) the Outline wiki backup CronJob dump initContainer (frontend/outline/app/backup-cronjob.yaml), pinned so pg_dump matches the cluster major. Minors/patches within 16 stay allowed for both.',
        'Issue: sigo-alumni backlog/infra/homelab-hosting/07 (wiki wave-2 backup continuity); stranded PR #2449 (v17) closed under this hold.',
        'Resume: MANUAL — lift only inside a planned postgres16→17 cluster-migration change that also bumps the outline dump image and verifies barman backups on the new major.',
        'Recorded: 2026-08-16 by claude (sigo-alumni session) per user call: wiki/cluster Postgres stays on 16.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['ghcr.io/cloudnative-pg/postgresql'],
      allowedVersions: '<17.0.0',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD cloudnative-pg chart: 0.30.0 and newer (operator 1.31.0+) — in-tree Barman backups removed.',
        'Reason: CNPG operator 1.31.0 REMOVES native (in-tree) barmanObjectStore support (deprecation notice updated in the 1.30.0 release notes: removal moved from 1.30 to 1.31). Our cluster16.yaml + cluster16-pgvecto.yaml still back up to s3://cnpg-haynesops via in-tree barmanObjectStore. Taking chart 0.30.0 (= operator 1.31.0) WITHOUT first migrating to the Barman Cloud Plugin (ObjectStore CR + cluster plugin config) would SILENTLY STOP all WAL archiving + base backups. The chart minor tracks the operator minor 1:1 (0.29.0 = 1.30.0, 0.30.0 = 1.31.0), so 0.29.x patches (operator 1.30.x) stay allowed.',
        'Issue: https://cloudnative-pg.io/documentation/1.30/release_notes/v1.30/ (in-tree barman removal in 1.31); https://github.com/cloudnative-pg/plugin-barman-cloud',
        'Resume: MANUAL — lift ONLY after migrating cluster16*.yaml from in-tree barmanObjectStore to the Barman Cloud Plugin (ObjectStore CR + spec.plugins) and verifying a Backup completes on the plugin path. Then widen this bound by hand.',
        'Recorded: 2026-07-05 by claude after taking chart 0.29.0 (operator 1.30.0, PR #1910). Related: .agents/runbooks/tier4-component-playbooks.md (cnpg backup-plugin migration watch); memory renovate-automation-roadmap.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['helm'],
      matchPackageNames: ['cloudnative-pg'],
      allowedVersions: '<0.30.0',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD docker.io/library/node majors: ride the 22 LTS ("Jod") line until its EOL — splash-screen build shim only.',
        'Reason: the ONLY consumer is the authentik `web-dist-lower` initContainer (PLAN-042) — a build-time npm/lightningcss CSS-flattening shim for the splash screen. Runs at pod init, serves no traffic, works on Node 22; a major runtime bump there is churn with zero payoff. The `22-bookworm-slim` tag rolls new 22.x patch builds on image pull, so security fixes inside the LTS line still arrive with no PRs at all.',
        'Issue: https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases — Node 22 "Jod" is LTS, maintenance ends 2027-04-30; Node 24 is the next LTS (ends ~2028-04).',
        'Resume: MANUAL — bump the initContainer tag to the then-current LTS (24-bookworm-slim) before 2027-04-30. If node ever gains a consumer outside the authentik helmrelease, split this hold per-consumer.',
        'Recorded: 2026-07-17 by claude per user call (PR #2054 closed): pin to the LTS line until EOL rather than chase majors for a build-only script.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['docker.io/library/node'],
      allowedVersions: '<23',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD coredns chart: 1.47.0 (CoreDNS 1.14.6) — Go-resolver A-lookups intermittently get empty answers.',
        'Reason: since the 1.47.0 roll (2026-07-30 04:01 ET, #2305) Go clients cluster-wide (flux source-controller, kyverno admission, loki, alertmanager, authentik outposts) intermittently receive NOERROR with an EMPTY A answer while AAAA resolves — the v4-only cluster then dials [v6]:443 → ENETUNREACH (~470/day). Real impact: kyverno cosign fetches fail → admission BLOCKS frontend Pods/Jobs. Reproduced with a stdlib-Go canary (90s episodes of dur_ms<5 server-answered empty-A); dig-shaped probes stayed clean for 50k+ queries because the autopath+cache path only fires on ndots search-expanded parallel A/AAAA queries, which dig never sends. Suspected cache/prefetch/serve_stale/autopath regression in CoreDNS 1.14.6.',
        'Issue: https://github.com/coredns/coredns/issues/8390 (filed 2026-08-04; local evidence: https://github.com/thaynes43/haynes-ops/pull/2332#issuecomment-5178557837). CONFIRMED causal by revert: ~470 errs/day to zero across all meters.',
        'Resume: MANUAL — lift after an upstream fix ships in a chart release AND the go-canary (PR #2335) soaks clean against it; or delete this hold in a roll-forward PR if the revert exonerates 1.47.0.',
        'Recorded: 2026-08-04 by claude (dev-env agent). Related: PR #2332 #2334 #2335; memory dns-canary-mission-state.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['ghcr.io/coredns/charts/coredns'],
      allowedVersions: '<1.47.0',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD postgres (plain docker.io library image): 18 and newer — the only consumer is vexa\'s bundled Postgres StatefulSet, which cannot cross a major in place.',
        'Reason: kubernetes/main/apps/ai/vexa/chart/values.yaml pins `postgres:17-alpine` on a bound 10Gi RWO PVC. The official image refuses to start on a PGDATA initialised by an older major, so a Renovate bump to 18 CrashLoopBackOffs the pod and takes vexa (meeting transcripts) down until it is reverted. There is no pg_upgrade tooling in the vendored chart. Minors/patches within 17 stay allowed. This is NOT the CNPG clusters — those are held separately above.',
        'Issue: none upstream — documented image behaviour (https://github.com/docker-library/docs/blob/master/postgres/README.md#pgdata). Stranded PR #1825 (v18, targeted archive/) closed without merging.',
        'Resume: MANUAL — lift only inside a planned vexa dump/restore (pg_dumpall from 17, fresh PGDATA on 18, restore, verify GET /meetings) change.',
        'Recorded: 2026-09-21 by claude per the 2026-09-12 backlog review. Related: memory renovate-backlog-landmines-2026-09.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['postgres', 'docker.io/postgres', 'docker.io/library/postgres'],
      allowedVersions: '<18',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'DISABLED vexaai/* images: digest-pinned as ONE set, bumped by hand — never by Renovate.',
        'Reason: upstream ships every vexa image on a floating tag (`v012`, or no tag at all for vexa-bot / v012-mcp). After the 2026-09-12 -> 09-16 drift incident (#2944: meeting-api pulled a build that needed MIGRATION-0005, every GET /meetings returned 500 for four days) all of them are pinned by digest in vexa/app/helmrelease.yaml (postRenderers + runtime.browserImage) and vexa/app/mcp.yaml, with the rule "re-vendor the chart, update ALL digests together, run upstream MIGRATION-000N FIRST". A Renovate digest PR moves ONE image, skips the schema step, lands under the ai/** auto-merge allowlist, and for the tagless pins re-resolves against `latest`. It also cannot resolve v012-mcp at all, which left a permanent "Package lookup failures" warning on the dashboard.',
        'Issue: https://github.com/thaynes43/haynes-ops/pull/2944',
        'Resume: MANUAL — re-enable only if upstream starts publishing immutable version tags, and then as a single group with automerge off.',
        'Recorded: 2026-09-21 by claude.',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['/(^|/)vexaai//'],
      enabled: false,
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD huggingface-hub: 2.0.0 and newer — drops the transitive httpx dependency that scripts/audio-authoring/test_service.py imports directly.',
        "Reason: huggingface-hub 2.0.0 replaces its HTTP stack with httpx2 (per the v2.0.0 release notes: 'clients and transport exceptions now come from httpx2/httpcore2 instead of httpx/httpcore'). httpx is NOT a direct dependency in scripts/audio-authoring/requirements.txt — it rides in transitively via huggingface-hub 1.x's own HTTP stack. test_service.py (the Dockerfile's `target: test` smoke test, run by .github/workflows/audio-authoring-build.yml with no network) does `import httpx` and calls httpx.get/Client/AsyncClient directly against the service's own /healthz and /readyz. On 2.0.0 that transitive httpx is gone, so the test image fails at run time with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named httpx` — confirmed from the failing build-and-push run's log, not a flaky/transient failure.",
        'Issue: https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface_hub/releases/tag/v2.0.0 (migration guide: https://huggingface.co/docs/huggingface_hub/main/en/concepts/migration_v2)',
        'Resume: MANUAL — lift only in a change that also closes the httpx gap: either pin httpx as an explicit direct dependency in requirements.txt, or migrate test_service.py to httpx2. Verify with a green build-and-push run before widening this bound.',
        'Recorded: 2026-09-28 by claude. Related: PR #3019 (merged, huggingface-hub 1.33.0 — the last 1.x release); PR #3180 (2.0.0, closed: build-and-push failed on the httpx ModuleNotFoundError).',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['pypi'],
      matchPackageNames: ['huggingface-hub'],
      allowedVersions: '<2.0.0',
    },
    {
      description: [
        'HELD ghcr.io/thaynes43/dev-env v2.x: the v1 dev-env pins stay on 0.x — dev-env v2 publishes its agent image to the SAME package with 2.x.y tags.',
        'Reason: dev-env v2 (repo thaynes43/dev-env, ADR-001 Accepted 2026-10-06, KICKOFF B5) pushes ghcr.io/thaynes43/dev-env:2.x.y. Without this hold, the first 2.x tag makes Renovate open a v1 "upgrade" PR that would put the v1 pod (and dev-env-ops, and the vexa scribe-notes Job) on a v2 operator-era image. The v1 pins are 0.6.x; DESIGN-001 says "A Renovate rule holds the v1 HelmRelease below 2.0.0".',
        'Scope: matchFileNames limits the hold to the 7 v1 pins (dev/dev-env HelmRelease x3, upgrade-agent/dev-env-ops HelmRelease x3, ai/vexa scribe-notes-job.json x1 — that JSON is not scanned by any Renovate manager today and is bumped by hand with the others). A future v2 pin elsewhere in this repo is NOT held.',
        'Resume: MANUAL — plan 05 (v2 cutover) removes this rule, or re-scopes matchFileNames, in the same PR that repoints the v1 files at v2 (or retires them).',
        'Recorded: 2026-10-06 by claude (dev-env v2 saga). Related: autoMerge.json5 dev-env manual-merge carve-out (unchanged, still applies below 2.0.0).',
      ],
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['/thaynes43/dev-env$/'],
      matchFileNames: [
        'kubernetes/main/apps/dev/dev-env/**',
        'kubernetes/main/apps/upgrade-agent/dev-env-ops/**',
        'kubernetes/main/apps/ai/vexa/app/resources/scribe-notes-job.json',
      ],
      allowedVersions: '<2.0.0',
    },
    // LIFTED 2026-07-17: grafana/mcp-grafana 0.17.1/0.17.2 /healthz 403 hold removed.
    //   Root cause was NOT a probe-path regression but v0.17.1's new DNS-rebinding
    //   protection (Host/Origin validation on every route, 403 for non-loopback Host).
    //   Resolved durably in the helmrelease by passing `--allowed-hosts '*'` (service
    //   sits behind the trusted traefik-internal proxy). The fix is version-independent,
    //   so there is no bad VERSION left to blacklist — the accommodation, not a pin, is
    //   the resolution. 0.17.2+ now flows under Tier-2 auto-merge. If a future release
    //   renames/removes --allowed-hosts or flips the default --address to loopback-only,
    //   the probe/clients break again → re-add a hold and adjust the helmrelease args.
    //   Related: PR #2016 (0.17.1), #2081 (0.17.2); memory renovate-automation-roadmap.
    //
    // LIFTED 2026-09-21: numpy '<2.5.0' hold removed — its resume condition is met.
    //   The hold existed only because scripts/audio-authoring/Dockerfile (numpy's single
    //   consumer in this repo) was `FROM python:3.11-slim` and every numpy 2.5.x declares
    //   Requires-Python >=3.12, so pip could not resolve the bump at all. The same change
    //   that removes this hold moves that Dockerfile to `python:3.14-slim` and pins
    //   numpy==2.5.3 (cp314 manylinux_2_28 x86_64 wheels published), exactly as the hold's
    //   'Resume: MANUAL — lift only in the same change that moves the Dockerfile off
    //   python:3.11-slim' required. There is no bad numpy VERSION left to blacklist. If a
    //   future numpy raises its Python floor past the image base again, the symptom is the
    //   same instant build failure ("No matching distribution found") — bump the base image
    //   in the same PR rather than re-adding a hold.
    //   Related: PR #2890/#2891/#2895 (the original churn), #2915 (Renovate's python 3.14
    //   base bump, superseded here); memory renovate-backlog-landmines-2026-09.
  ],
}
